members.description:
What an `lx` call throws or rejects with, argument refusals included, so one `catch` handles it.
Branch on `code`, never on `message`; a refusal is `E_INVALID_ARG` with `data.argument`, `path`,
`expected` and `got`:

```ts
async function pickFolder() {
  try {
    return await lx.pick.directory()
  } catch (e) {
    if (e instanceof LxError && e.code === 'E_NOT_SUPPORTED') return null
    throw e
  }
}
```
The class the Logic runtime builds every host error from; the same class elsewhere (Node tests).

Define a page. Declare what it takes and returns at the top, then its
behaviour in one of two forms. `setup(page)` is the form for lifecycle
hooks and per-instance state: it runs once per instance, before `onLoad`,
and returns its hooks and `actions`. `actions: page => ({ … })` is the
short form for a page with only actions; it also runs once per instance.

```ts
export default definePage({
  params: type<{ id: string }>(),
  data: { order: null as Order | null },
  setup(page) {
    return {
      async onLoad({ id }) { const order = await load(id); page.update(d => { d.order = order; }); },
      actions: { close() { return page.close(); } },
    };
  },
});

export default definePage({
  data: { count: 0 },
  actions: page => ({ bump() { page.update(d => { d.count += 1; }); } }),
});
```

Shared Logic state: one value for every page of this lxapp, defined once at module scope.
Its value is JSON data, as page data is.

```ts
export const cart = defineStore({ items: [] as Item[] });
cart.update(d => { d.items.push(item); });
const count = cart.pick(c => c.items.length);
```

examples:
lx.app.moreActions.replace([
{ icon: 'public/feedback.svg', label: 'Feedback', onSelect: () => openFeedback() },
]);

const picked = await lx.host.banner.show({
  title: 'Run finished',
  actions: [{ id: 'open', label: 'Open', target: { page: 'run', params: { id: '42' } } }],
});

const task = lx.media.compressVideo(clip, { quality: 'medium' });
for await (const { fraction } of task) render(fraction);
const { path, size } = await task.result;

await lx.shell.sidebarActions.replace([
{ id: 'new', placement: 'header', icon: 'public/plus.svg', label: 'New', onSelect: () => createDraft() },
]);

members.description:
The handle of an lxapp live as a surface of its own, declared or not;
`undefined` when it is not. A live lxapp has one handle: `lx.surface.openApp`,
`lx.surface.app` and `lx.surface.declared` of the declaration that shows it return the same one.

examples:
lx.ui.toast('Saved', { tone: 'success' });
const busy = lx.ui.toast('Uploading…', { loading: true, durationMs: 60_000 });
busy.dismiss();

members.description:
The page that opened this one, by `lx.nav.go` or `lx.surface.openPage`;
absent for a root, a tab, after a restart, and while `setup` runs (read
it in a hook or an action).

types.description:
What `lx.shell.appDisplay.update` changes. Each key it carries is set;
`undefined`, `null` or `''` restores the default, and a key left out
keeps its value.

Result of `lx.clipboard.readText`. Branch on `status`.
A copied empty string is `{ status: 'ok', text: '' }`;
an image-only clipboard has no `text`.

fields.description:
How this update is applied. `store` opens the platform marketplace;
`direct` downloads and self-installs, the only case where
self-update is supported.

